---
title: "The program's folders"
flm:
  use: [flmdoc]
  math: false
---
The folders the program reads: the search path of extensions, the folder of the citation cache, the image folders.

\section*{Search path}

The folders in which an extension is looked for, in the order searched:

\begin{itemize}
\item \verbcode{ext} (-{}-extensions-dir)
\item \verbcode{~/.flm/extensions} (the user's folder), which does not exist
\end{itemize}

\section*{Citation cache}

The folder of the citation cache: \verbcode{_cache}, which does not exist.

\section*{Image folders}

The folders in which an image's file is looked for:

\begin{itemize}
\item \verbcode{.}
\end{itemize}

Each folder is relative to the folder of the file that writes the image, or absolute.

